<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 10, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">Launched <a href="/storefront" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/storefront</a>, a feature page for the Breeder Storefront that every BreederHQ breeder gets at marketplace.breederhq.com/breeders/&lt;slug&gt;. The page explains that the Storefront fills in from breeding records and feeds the waitlist and sales pipeline, so a breeder does not need a separately built, hosted and hand-updated website.</p>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">Sections</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1">
    <li>Hero with the Stoneridge Heritage Farms storefront header; primary button "Apply And Book A Tour" to /pricing, secondary "Browse Real Storefronts" to the live marketplace breeder directory.</li>
    <li>The breeder website problem, what updates itself, programs, breeder-attested records panels (herd health, parasite program, linear appraisal, dairy production), the waitlist-to-placement pipeline, a three-option comparison table (no competitor named), two doors (domain forwarding at the registrar, or the free embed widget), FAQ and final call to action.</li>
    <li>Domain claim is forwarding only; hosting a Storefront on a breeder's own domain is not offered. The FAQ tells breeders to update the forwarding target if they change their Storefront address (the old address redirects for 14 days).</li>
    <li>Screenshots are trimmed copies of the demo storefront in <code>public/images/screenshots/storefront/</code>, cropped to avoid demo-data defects.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">SEO and AI</h3>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-2">FAQ schema through the BaseLayout <code>faqs</code> prop. New entries in <code>public/llms.txt</code> and <code>public/okf/product.md</code>.</p>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">Internal links</h3>
